  "content": [
    {
      "text": "Rachel was beautiful and well favoured, Gen. 29:17. garments … for glory and for beauty, Ex. 28:2 (28:2–40). ruddy … of a beautiful countenance, 1 Sam. 16:12. worship … in the beauty of holiness, 1 Chr. 16:29 (Ps. 29:2). garnished … with precious stones for beauty, 2 Chr. 3:6. beautify the house of the Lord, Ezra 7:27. Esther … was fair and beautiful, Esth. 2:7. behold the beauty of the Lord, Ps. 27:4. Beautiful for situation … is mount Zion, Ps. 48:2. Out of Zion, the perfection of beauty, Ps. 50:2. beauty of the Lord … be upon us, Ps. 90:17. he will beautify the meek with salvation, Ps. 149:4. beauty of old men is the gray head, Prov. 20:29. beauty is vain, Prov. 31:30. He hath made every thing beautiful, Eccl. 3:11. branch of the Lord be beautiful, Isa. 4:2. eyes shall see the king in his beauty, Isa. 33:17. How beautiful upon the mountains are the feet of him that bringeth good tidings, Isa. 52:7. no beauty that we should desire him, Isa. 53:2 (Mosiah 14:2). to beautify the place of my sanctuary, Isa. 60:13. give unto them beauty for ashes, Isa. 61:3. Our holy and our beautiful house, Isa. 64:11 (64:9–12).",
